Native firmware tests (no ESP32 required)
========================================

From the repository root, after PlatformIO downloads the display dependency:

clang++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
  -Itest/native_stubs -Isrc \
  -I'.pio/libdeps/esp32s3/GFX Library for Arduino/src' \
  test/poetry_native.cpp src/app.cpp src/letters.cpp \
  -o /tmp/poetry-native-test
/tmp/poetry-native-test

These tests compile the production app state machine, animation renderer,
layout, motion, and perspective math. Only Arduino, touch, display output,
random seed and clock interfaces are stubbed. They check explicit line breaks,
centering, twelve small-font layouts and random eligible selection, overflow rejection, all eight animation styles,
edge-on projection, near-plane clipping, mixed words/letters, faint full-screen echoes that disappear from the reading corpus, continuous 0.55 s assembly, overlapping 0.65 s scene changes, retained incoming motion clocks, 468-particle stress cases and clustered/stream/patch formation occupancy, variable scale that settles to1, safe multiword fragments, seeded independent drift, randomized grouping, and staggered particle timing,
indefinite moving/reading states, and held-finger behavior.

This is not a hardware or performance test. Use ./pio run for an ESP32 build
and verify frame rate and touch behavior on the actual board when available.
